    "answer": "NEI",
    "explanation": "The claim concerns the diagnostic significance of the ZMIZ1::ABL1 fusion in B-lymphoblastic Leukemia/lymphoma, BCR-ABL1–like, specifically regarding pediatric onset and negative significance. The provided evidence (pmid-26324363:f01) describes a Phase 1 study of the pan-FGFR inhibitor JNJ-42756493 in solid tumors, focusing on FGFR pathway aberrations (specifically FGFR2-BICC1 and FGFR2-CASP7 fusions). There is no mention of ABL1 fusions, ZMIZ1, B-lymphoblastic Leukemia/lymphoma, BCR-ABL1–like, pediatric onset, or diagnostic significance in the provided text. The evidence is entirely irrelevant to the claim.",
